[01:12.10] Not forever on earth; only a little while here
[04:33.64] Be it jade, it shatters
[04:39.60] Be it gold, it breaks
[04:43.72] Be it a quetzal feather, it tears apart
[04:52.42] Not forever on earth; only a little while here
[05:04.36] Like a painting, we will be erased
[05:10.80] Like a flower, we will dry up here on earth
[05:22.76] Like plumed vestments of the precious bird
[05:25.98] That precious bird with the agile neck
[05:35.00] We will come to an end
[06:40.14] He goes his way singing, offering flowers
[06:46.78] And his words rain down
[06:51.32] Like jade and quetzal plumes
[06:55.24] Is this what pleases the Giver of Life?
[07:39.08] Is that the only truth on earth?
